{"id": "EUVD-2026-103825", "enisaUuid": "0e868173-e3fe-3089-8544-8a34b2310443", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nEDAC/altera: Drop __init from ECC setup paths for re-probe safety\n\nSashiko reports:\n\n\"Does suppressing sysfs unbinding fully prevent the execution of freed __init\nmemory? If altr_sysmgr_regmap_lookup_by_phandle() returns -EPROBE_DEFER, the\nprobe is deferred until after __init memory is freed.\"\n\nThe a10 EDAC .setup callbacks (sdmmc, ethernet, nand, dma, usb, qspi) and\ntheir helpers (altr_init_a10_ecc_device_type, altr_init_a10_ecc_block) were\nmarked __init. These run from the probe path, which may execute after init\nmemory is freed -- e.g. a probe deferred via -EPROBE_DEFER that only succeeds\nonce a late/module dependency appears, or a manual unbind/rebind. Calling\n__init code then dereferences freed memory. Remove __init so these functions\nremain valid at runtime.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:47:24", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:24:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9846b85c2eb8b749c3f14bdcc31b1070f6aabba8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4ec26cb7984740941892ad21fa974963c198bfaa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b62a264163ca51bee04785c581344751812395df"], "aliases": ["GHSA-rrjq-wrm9-p6gm", "CVE-2026-98740"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e0e04b1-e86b-32f0-93d4-94b213352f95", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.2"}, {"id": "7519f0c6-6e33-3fdd-a04b-e7327ee08163", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "788586efd116d6d7d05985881eda503333e702b4 <b62a264163ca51bee04785c581344751812395df"}, {"id": "8b47f047-b55a-3f3b-b07e-deba24d1830f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "788586efd116d6d7d05985881eda503333e702b4 <4ec26cb7984740941892ad21fa974963c198bfaa"}, {"id": "b103ca1e-9f8a-3bab-9d71-d537add1f5ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "c9581734-c86a-3b67-b8d7-10c50264e690", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "eaa46c6e-f46b-3de8-883a-2107dc48ca13", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "fadf62ea-0fd3-3798-8a95-14bd2253b75e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "fce8183a-9505-33d6-b79c-40465dbf9acd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "788586efd116d6d7d05985881eda503333e702b4 <9846b85c2eb8b749c3f14bdcc31b1070f6aabba8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b122c726-2d46-396c-abb0-dba3d80edaf2", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}